% Knee Orthoses: LCD L33318 and its Policy Article A52465 (DME MACs). A
% policy program of the DMEPOS model: it includes dmepos.le (orders,
% delivery, benefit category, continued need, refills) and states when a
% claim for a knee orthosis is REASONABLE AND NECESSARY:
%   - an elastic knee orthosis with joints (L1810, L1812, L1820, L1821): an
%     ambulatory beneficiary with weakness or deformity of the knee who
%     requires stabilization;
%   - a locking or rigid knee orthosis (L1831, L1836): a nonfixed flexion or
%     extension contracture of the knee (at least 10 degrees of movement on
%     passive range of motion testing; group 1);
%   - an immobilizer (L1830): a recent injury to or surgery on the knee
%     (groups 2 or 4);
%   - adjustable knee joints (L1832, L1833): a recent injury or surgery, or an
%     ambulatory beneficiary with knee instability (group 4);
%   - the Swedish type orthosis (L1850): ambulatory, knee instability due to
%     genu recurvatum (group 5);
%   - the rotation control orthoses (L1843, L1845, L1851, L1852): objective
%     knee instability in an ambulatory beneficiary (group 4), or a recent
%     injury or surgery (groups 2 or 4), or medial or lateral tibiofemoral
%     osteoarthritis (group 6) with criteria a-d;
%   - the custom fabricated orthoses (L1834, L1840, L1844, L1846, L1860): the
%     criteria of their prefabricated counterparts (L1840: instability due to
%     internal ligamentous disruption, group 3) and a documented physical
%     characteristic requiring custom fabrication;
%   - an addition: separately payable with its base orthosis (the LCD's
%     tables), the base and the addition reasonable and necessary; the heavy
%     duty joints (L2385, L2395) for a beneficiary over 300 pounds; the
%     replacement soft interface (K0672) two per year after the first year.
% The air bladder orthoses (L1847, L1848) are never covered ("no proven
% clinical benefit"): no rule concludes them. A custom fabricated orthosis
% for the contracture of a nonambulatory beneficiary is never covered either
% (no rule concludes one: the contracture codes L1831, L1836 are
% prefabricated). The concentric torsion mechanism (L2999), whose text the
% knee LCD repeats from the AFO/KAFO LCD, is decided by afo_kafo.le. The
% benefit is not durable medical equipment: the Policy Article places knee
% orthoses under the Medicare braces benefit (Social Security Act
% §1861(s)(9)).
%
% How the criteria are read. What the record states is a scenario fact: the
% diagnosis code, the movement on passive range of motion testing (a number),
% the ambulatory status, the documented weakness, deformity, recent injury
% or recent surgery (the shared template "the medical record of B documents
% C"), the varus or valgus adjustment of the orthosis, the willingness to use
% it, the beneficiary's weight, the examination and imaging documentation.
% What someone finds is the judged template of dmepos.le. The findings this
% policy reads, and the criterion each stands for:
%   knee stabilization required (L1810-L1821); knee instability (the
%   objective instability of L1832/L1833, L1843-L1852, L1850/L1860, L1840 —
%   the diagnosis group tells the kind); osteoarthritis limits function
%   (criterion b: pain or a reduction in mobility or function due to the
%   osteoarthritis); custom fabrication required (the documented physical
%   characteristic: deformity of the leg or knee, the size of thigh and calf,
%   minimal muscle mass — ONE finding); addition medically necessary.
% Three record templates are also templates of afo_kafo.le (the ambulatory
% status, the orthotist's records, the diagnosis on the claim line): they are
% declared here, as candidates for dmepos.le, rather than by including
% afo_kafo.le — its documentation rule, guarded by "the policy of the claim
% is afo_kafo", fails on every knee claim and would make "stage" blame the
% applicability section.
%
% The Policy Article's ICD-10 table (sources/icd10/A52465_icd10_covered.csv,
% 9,621 rows, loaded as the table knee_icd10), whose groups the LCD names:
% group 1 (knee contractures) serves L1831, L1836; groups 2 and 4 (a recent
% injury or surgery) serve L1830, L1832, L1833, L1834, L1843-L1852, L1844,
% L1846; group 3 (internal ligamentous disruption) serves L1840; group 4
% (knee instability) serves L1832, L1833, L1843-L1852, L1844, L1846; group 5
% (genu recurvatum) serves L1850, L1860; group 6 (tibiofemoral
% osteoarthritis) serves L1843-L1852, L1844, L1846. The Article's text in
% sources/ carries no "Group N" paragraphs; the mapping is the LCD's. A code
% may be in several groups (the osteoarthritis codes M17.x are in groups 2,
% 4 and 6).
%
% The payment conditions the Policy Article adds ("Policy specific
% documentation requirements"), in section remedy: for L1832, L1833 and L1850
% and for the rotation control orthoses managing instability, the joint
% laxity tests performed and the examination findings supporting objective
% laxity (and, for the latter, the ambulatory status); for the osteoarthritis
% route the ambulatory status, the symptoms, the physical examination and an
% imaging report (the willingness to use the orthosis is already criterion
% d); for a custom fabricated orthosis the orthotist's functional
% evaluation; for the base codes the diagnosis code on the claim line. The
% Article requires the laxity documentation of L1832, L1833 and L1850
% without condition; this program requires it when the recorded finding is
% knee instability (the LCD: "objective knee instability must be supported by
% documentation"), so an L1832 after knee surgery needs none.
%
% Not modelled: the additions not separately payable or incompatible with a
% base (denied as incorrect coding, no rule concludes them); the OTS versus
% custom fitted coding; the hospital and SNF payment rules; the reasonable
% useful lifetime and replacement rules; the KX/GA/GZ/RT/LT modifiers;
% repairs (L4205, L4210); the PDAC coding verification. One year is read as
% 365 days.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    % the record
    % candidate for dmepos.le (also a template of afo_kafo.le)
    *a beneficiary* is ambulatory; undefined.
    % candidate for dmepos.le (also a template of afo_kafo.le)
    the records of the orthotist include a functional evaluation corroborating the need for custom fabrication of *an item*; undefined.
    % candidate for dmepos.le (also a template of afo_kafo.le)
    *a claim* states the diagnosis code of the beneficiary; undefined.
    the movement of the knee of *a beneficiary* on passive range of motion testing is *a number* degrees; undefined.
    the compartment adjustment of *an item* is *an adjustment*; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* expresses a willingness to use *an item*; undefined.
    the medical record of *a beneficiary* documents the joint laxity tests performed on the knee; undefined.
    the medical record of *a beneficiary* documents examination findings supporting objective joint laxity; undefined.
    the medical record of *a beneficiary* documents the ambulatory status; undefined.
    the medical record of *a beneficiary* documents the symptoms due to tibiofemoral osteoarthritis; undefined.
    the medical record of *a beneficiary* documents a physical examination of the knee; undefined.
    the medical record of *a beneficiary* includes an imaging report describing arthritic changes of the knee; undefined.
    the count of replacement soft interfaces furnished to *a beneficiary* in the year of *a claim* is *a number*; undefined.
    % the codes and the lists
    ICD10 code *a code* is in group *a group* of article *an article* as *a description* under table knee_icd10.
    addition *a code* is separately payable with base *an other code* under table knee_additions.
    *a condition* is a qualifying condition for a knee orthosis with joints.
    *a condition* is a documented recent knee injury.
    % derived
    *an item* is a custom fabricated knee orthosis.
    *an item* is an addition to a knee orthosis.
    *an item* is a heavy duty knee joint.
    *an item* is a knee orthosis with examination documentation.
    *an item* is a knee orthosis requiring the diagnosis code on the claim line.
    *an item* meets the knee orthosis coverage criteria for *a beneficiary*.
    *a beneficiary* has a nonfixed knee contracture.
    *a beneficiary* has had a recent injury to the knee.
    *a beneficiary* has objective knee instability.
    *a beneficiary* has knee instability due to genu recurvatum.
    *a beneficiary* meets the criteria for a knee orthosis with adjustable joints.
    *a beneficiary* meets the criteria for a rotation control knee orthosis with *an item*.
    *a beneficiary* meets the osteoarthritis criteria for *an item*.
    the knee custom fabrication criteria are met for *an item*.
    the addition specific criteria are met for *an item*.
    the knee examination documentation is met for *an item*.
    the knee custom fabrication documentation is met for *an item*.
    the knee claim line diagnosis requirement is met for *a claim*.

% The Policy Article's ICD-10 table (the CSV columns bind to the template's
% arguments in order: code, group, article, description).
the table knee_icd10 is loaded from sources/icd10/A52465_icd10_covered.csv, with all matches:
    code | group | article | description

