the knowledge base knee_orthoses includes these resources:
    dmepos.

the knowledge base knee_orthoses includes:

LCD L33318 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=33318".
the text of LCD L33318 is at "sources/lcd/L33318.txt".
Policy Article A52465 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52465".
the text of Policy Article A52465 is at "sources/article/A52465.txt".

% What the items are, by code (Policy Article A52465, LCD L33318).
rule ko_custom_fabricated_device with provenance Policy Article A52465,
        confer "For a custom fabricated orthosis (L1834, L1840, L1844, L1846, L1860), there must be detailed documentation in the treating practitioner’s records":
an item is a custom fabricated knee orthosis
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L1834", "L1840", "L1844", "L1846", "L1860"].

rule ko_addition_device with provenance Policy Article A52465,
        confer "L-coded additions to knee orthoses (L2275, L2320, L2330, L2385, L2390, L2395, L2397, L2405, L2415, L2425, L2430, L2492, L2750, L2755, L2780, L2785, L2795, L2800, L2810, L2820, L2830, K0672) will be denied as noncovered when the base orthosis is noncovered":
an item is an addition to a knee orthosis
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L2275", "L2320", "L2330", "L2385", "L2390", "L2395", "L2397", "L2405", "L2415", "L2425", "L2430", "L2492", "L2750", "L2755", "L2780", "L2785", "L2795", "L2800", "L2810", "L2820", "L2830"].

rule ko_heavy_duty_joint with provenance LCD L33318,
        confer "Heavy duty knee joint codes (L2385, L2395) are covered only for beneficiaries who weigh more than 300 pounds":
an item is a heavy duty knee joint
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L2385", "L2395"].

% The base codes whose diagnosis code the Article requires on the claim line.
rule ko_claim_line_codes with provenance Policy Article A52465,
        confer "The supplier must include on the claim line the diagnosis code(s) for HCPCS codes L1830, L1831, L1832, L1833, L1834, L1836, L1840, L1843, L1844, L1845, L1846, L1850, L1851, L1852 and L1860":
an item is a knee orthosis requiring the diagnosis code on the claim line
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L1830", "L1831", "L1832", "L1833", "L1834", "L1836", "L1840", "L1843", "L1844", "L1845", "L1846", "L1850", "L1851", "L1852", "L1860"].

% The base codes the Article's documentation requirements name.
rule ko_examination_documentation_codes with provenance Policy Article A52465,
        confer "For a knee orthosis with adjustable knee joints or a prefabricated Swedish type knee orthosis (L1832, L1833, L1850), the medical records must include documentation of the beneficiary’s physical examination of the affected knee(s), including all of the following":
an item is a knee orthosis with examination documentation
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L1832", "L1833", "L1850", "L1843", "L1844", "L1845", "L1846", "L1851", "L1852"].

% Two criteria that the documentation requirements (section remedy) read as
% well as the coverage rules: before the first section, so that a claim
% failing its documentation is not blamed on the question.
% A recent injury to or surgery on the knee: documented in the record, with
% a diagnosis of the Article's group 2 or 4.
rule ko_recent_injury with provenance LCD L33318,
        confer "The beneficiary has had a recent injury to or a surgical procedure on the knee(s) (refer to the Groups 2 or Group 4 ICD-10 Codes in the LCD-related Policy Article)":
a beneficiary has had a recent injury to the knee
    if the medical record of the beneficiary documents a condition
    and the condition is a documented recent knee injury
    and the diagnosis code of the beneficiary is a code
    and ICD10 code the code is in group a group of article "A52465" as a description under table knee_icd10
    and the group is in [2, 4].

recent knee injury is a documented recent knee injury,
    as stated in LCD L33318, confer "has had a recent injury to or a surgical procedure on the knee(s)".
recent knee surgery is a documented recent knee injury,
    as stated in LCD L33318, confer "has had a recent injury to or a surgical procedure on the knee(s)".

% Criterion 3 of the rotation control orthoses: osteoarthritis with a-d.
rule ko_osteoarthritis_criteria with provenance LCD L33318,
        confer "The beneficiary is experiencing pain or reduction in their mobility and/or function secondary to the medial or lateral tibiofemoral osteoarthritis":
a beneficiary meets the osteoarthritis criteria for an item
    if the diagnosis code of the beneficiary is a code
    and ICD10 code the code is in group 6 of article "A52465" as a description under table knee_icd10
    and the beneficiary is ambulatory
    and the finding osteoarthritis limits function about the beneficiary is established
    and the compartment adjustment of the item is an adjustment
    and the adjustment is in [varus, valgus]
    and the beneficiary expresses a willingness to use the item.

% The codes this policy decides — outside the section checklist: a claim
% of another policy fails here without failing its own applicability.
% The codes this policy decides: the prefabricated and custom fabricated
% knee orthoses, the additions, the replacement soft interface. The L-coded
% additions are also additions of afo_kafo.le: both policies decide them,
% and the base orthosis they are provided with tells which rule applies.
rule ko_codes with provenance Policy Article A52465,
        confer "Knee orthoses (KO) are covered under the Medicare braces benefit (Social Security Act §1861(s)(9))":
the policy for code a code is knee_orthoses
    if the code is in ["L1810", "L1812", "L1820", "L1821", "L1830", "L1831", "L1832", "L1833", "L1834", "L1836", "L1840", "L1843", "L1844", "L1845", "L1846", "L1847", "L1848", "L1850", "L1851", "L1852", "L1860", "L2275", "L2320", "L2330", "L2385", "L2390", "L2395", "L2397", "L2405", "L2415", "L2425", "L2430", "L2492", "L2750", "L2755", "L2780", "L2785", "L2795", "L2800", "L2810", "L2820", "L2830", "K0672"].

section applicability is:

% The benefit: not durable medical equipment but the braces benefit of
% Social Security Act §1861(s)(9).
rule ko_benefit with provenance Policy Article A52465,
        confer "Knee orthoses (KO) are covered under the Medicare braces benefit (Social Security Act §1861(s)(9))":
the benefit category of code a code is braces
    if the policy for code the code is knee_orthoses.

section question is:

% A claim for a base orthosis: the orthosis meets the criteria of its code.
rule ko_base_orthosis with provenance LCD L33318,
        confer "Claims for L1832, L1833, L1843, L1845, L1850, L1851 or L1852 will be denied as not reasonable and necessary when the beneficiary does not meet the above criteria for coverage":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the item meets the knee orthosis coverage criteria for the beneficiary.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Prefabricated knee orthoses.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule ko_elastic_with_joints with provenance LCD L33318,
        confer "A knee orthosis with joints (L1810, L1812) or knee orthosis with condylar pads and joints with or without patellar control (L1820, L1821) are covered for ambulatory beneficiaries who have weakness or deformity of the knee and require stabilization":
an item meets the knee orthosis coverage criteria for a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L1810", "L1812", "L1820", "L1821"]
    and the beneficiary is ambulatory
    and the medical record of the beneficiary documents a condition
    and the condition is a qualifying condition for a knee orthosis with joints
    and the finding knee stabilization required about the beneficiary is established.

weakness of the knee is a qualifying condition for a knee orthosis with joints,
    as stated in LCD L33318, confer "ambulatory beneficiaries who have weakness or deformity of the knee and require stabilization".
deformity of the knee is a qualifying condition for a knee orthosis with joints,
    as stated in LCD L33318, confer "ambulatory beneficiaries who have weakness or deformity of the knee and require stabilization".

rule ko_contracture with provenance LCD L33318,
        confer "A knee orthosis with a locking knee joint (L1831) or a rigid knee orthosis (L1836) is covered for beneficiaries with flexion or extension contractures of the knee with movement on passive range of motion testing of at least 10 degrees (i.e., a nonfixed contracture)":
an item meets the knee orthosis coverage criteria for a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L1831", "L1836"]
    and the beneficiary has a nonfixed knee contracture.

rule ko_nonfixed_contracture with provenance LCD L33318,
        confer "with movement on passive range of motion testing of at least 10 degrees (i.e., a nonfixed contracture) (r efer to the Group 1 ICD-10 Codes in the LCD-related Policy Article )":
a beneficiary has a nonfixed knee contracture
    if the diagnosis code of the beneficiary is a code
    and ICD10 code the code is in group 1 of article "A52465" as a description under table knee_icd10
    and the movement of the knee of the beneficiary on passive range of motion testing is a number degrees
    and the number >= 10.

rule ko_immobilizer with provenance LCD L33318,
        confer "An immobilizer knee orthosis without joints (L1830) is covered for a beneficiary who has had a recent injury to or a surgical procedure on the knee(s)":
an item meets the knee orthosis coverage criteria for a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "L1830"
    and the beneficiary has had a recent injury to the knee.

rule ko_adjustable_joints with provenance LCD L33318,
        confer "A knee orthosis with adjustable knee joints (L1832, L1833) is covered if one of the following criteria is met":
an item meets the knee orthosis coverage criteria for a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L1832", "L1833"]
    and the beneficiary meets the criteria for a knee orthosis with adjustable joints.

rule ko_adjustable_after_injury with provenance LCD L33318,
        confer "The beneficiary has had a recent injury to or a surgical procedure on the knee(s) (refer to the Groups 2 or Group 4 ICD-10 Codes in the LCD-related Policy Article)":
a beneficiary meets the criteria for a knee orthosis with adjustable joints
    if the beneficiary has had a recent injury to the knee.

rule ko_adjustable_instability with provenance LCD L33318,
        confer "The beneficiary is ambulatory and has knee instability (refer to the Group 4 ICD-10 Codes in the LCD-related Policy Article)":
a beneficiary meets the criteria for a knee orthosis with adjustable joints
    if the beneficiary is ambulatory
    and the beneficiary has objective knee instability.

% Objective knee instability: the finding, with a diagnosis of group 4.
rule ko_objective_instability with provenance LCD L33318,
        confer "objective knee instability must be supported by documentation of the beneficiary’s physical examination including the joint laxity test(s) performed":
a beneficiary has objective knee instability
    if the finding knee instability about the beneficiary is established
    and the diagnosis code of the beneficiary is a code
    and ICD10 code the code is in group 4 of article "A52465" as a description under table knee_icd10.

rule ko_swedish with provenance LCD L33318,
        confer "A prefabricated Swedish type knee orthosis (L1850) is covered for a beneficiary who is ambulatory and has knee instability due to genu recurvatum - hyperextended knee, congenital or acquired (refer to the Group 5 ICD-10 Codes in the LCD-related Policy Article)":
an item meets the knee orthosis coverage criteria for a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "L1850"
    and the beneficiary is ambulatory
    and the beneficiary has knee instability due to genu recurvatum.

rule ko_genu_recurvatum with provenance LCD L33318,
        confer "has knee instability due to genu recurvatum - hyperextended knee, congenital or acquired (refer to the Group 5 ICD-10 Codes in the LCD-related Policy Article)":
a beneficiary has knee instability due to genu recurvatum
    if the finding knee instability about the beneficiary is established
    and the diagnosis code of the beneficiary is a code
    and ICD10 code the code is in group 5 of article "A52465" as a description under table knee_icd10.

rule ko_rotation_control with provenance LCD L33318,
        confer "A knee orthosis with single or double upright, adjustable flexion and extension joint, medial-lateral and rotation control, with or without varus/valgus adjustment (L1843, L1845, L1851, L1852) is covered if one of the following criteria (1-3) is met":
an item meets the knee orthosis coverage criteria for a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L1843", "L1845", "L1851", "L1852"]
    and the beneficiary meets the criteria for a rotation control knee orthosis with the item.

% Criterion 1.
rule ko_rotation_instability with provenance LCD L33318,
        confer "The beneficiary is ambulatory and has objective knee instability that must be supported by documentation of a physical examination including the joint laxity test(s) performed":
a beneficiary meets the criteria for a rotation control knee orthosis with an item
    if the beneficiary is ambulatory
    and the beneficiary has objective knee instability.

% Criterion 2.
rule ko_rotation_injury with provenance LCD L33318,
        confer "The beneficiary has had a recent injury to or a surgical procedure on the knee(s) (refer to the Groups 2 or Group 4 ICD-10 Codes in the LCD-related Policy Article)":
a beneficiary meets the criteria for a rotation control knee orthosis with an item
    if the beneficiary has had a recent injury to the knee.

% Criterion 3: osteoarthritis with a-d.
rule ko_rotation_osteoarthritis with provenance LCD L33318,
        confer "The beneficiary has a documented (see the POLICY SPECIFIC DOCUMENTATION REQUIREMENTS section in the LCD-related Policy Article) diagnosis of medial or lateral tibiofemoral osteoarthritis (refer to the Group 6 ICD-10 Codes in the LCD-related Policy Article), and meets all criteria (a-d)":
a beneficiary meets the criteria for a rotation control knee orthosis with an item
    if the beneficiary meets the osteoarthritis criteria for the item.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Custom fabricated knee orthoses.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule ko_custom_immobilizer with provenance LCD L33318,
        confer "A custom fabricated knee immobilizer without joints (L1834) is covered if criteria 1 and 2 are met":
an item meets the knee orthosis coverage criteria for a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "L1834"
    and the beneficiary has had a recent injury to the knee
    and the knee custom fabrication criteria are met for the item.

rule ko_derotation with provenance LCD L33318,
        confer "A custom fabricated derotation knee orthosis (L1840) is covered for instability due to internal ligamentous disruption of the knee ( refer to the Group 3 ICD-10 Codes in the LCD-related Policy Article )":
an item meets the knee orthosis coverage criteria for a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "L1840"
    and the finding knee instability about the beneficiary is established
    and the diagnosis code of the beneficiary is a code
    and ICD10 code the code is in group 3 of article "A52465" as a description under table knee_icd10
    and the knee custom fabrication criteria are met for the item.

rule ko_custom_adjustable with provenance LCD L33318,
        confer "A custom fabricated knee orthosis with an adjustable flexion and extension joint (L1844, L1846) is covered if criteria 1 and 2 are met":
an item meets the knee orthosis coverage criteria for a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L1844", "L1846"]
    and the beneficiary meets the criteria for a rotation control knee orthosis with the item
    and the knee custom fabrication criteria are met for the item.

rule ko_supracondylar with provenance LCD L33318,
        confer "A custom fabricated knee orthosis with a modified supracondylar prosthetic socket (L1860) is covered for a beneficiary who is ambulatory and has knee instability due to genu recurvatum - hyperextended knee ( refer to the Group 5 ICD-10 Codes in the LCD-related Policy Article )":
an item meets the knee orthosis coverage criteria for a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "L1860"
    and the beneficiary is ambulatory
    and the beneficiary has knee instability due to genu recurvatum
    and the knee custom fabrication criteria are met for the item.

% The general criterion of a custom fabricated orthosis: ONE finding for the
% documented physical characteristic (deformity, size, minimal muscle mass).
rule ko_custom_criteria with provenance LCD L33318,
        confer "A custom fabricated orthosis is covered when there is a documented physical characteristic which requires the use of a custom fabricated orthosis instead of a prefabricated orthosis":
the knee custom fabrication criteria are met for an item
    if the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the finding custom fabrication required about the beneficiary is established.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Additions and the replacement soft interface.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule ko_additions with provenance LCD L33318,
        confer "Addition codes will be denied as not reasonable and necessary if the base orthosis is not reasonable and necessary or the addition is not reasonable and necessary":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is an addition to a knee orthosis
    and the item is an accessory of a device
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the HCPCS code of the device is an other code
    and addition the code is separately payable with base the other code under table knee_additions
    and the device is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the device meets the knee orthosis coverage criteria for the beneficiary
    and the finding addition medically necessary about the beneficiary is established
    and the addition specific criteria are met for the item.

rule ko_heavy_duty_weight with provenance LCD L33318,
        confer "Heavy duty knee joint codes (L2385, L2395) are covered only for beneficiaries who weigh more than 300 pounds":
the addition specific criteria are met for an item
    if the item is a heavy duty knee joint
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the weight of the beneficiary is a number pounds
    and the number > 300.

% any other addition has no criterion of its own: a device of this model
rule ko_no_addition_specific_criteria:
the addition specific criteria are met for an item
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and it is not the case that
        the item is a heavy duty knee joint.

rule ko_replacement_interface with provenance LCD L33318,
        confer "Coverage of a removable soft interface (K0672) is limited to a maximum of two (2) per year beginning one (1) year after the date of service for initial issuance of the orthosis":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is "K0672"
    and the item is an accessory of a device
    and the device is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the device meets the knee orthosis coverage criteria for the beneficiary
    and the device was delivered on a date
    and the date of service of the claim is an other date
    and the other date is a number days after the date
    and the number >= 365
    and the item is furnished to the beneficiary
    and the count of replacement soft interfaces furnished to the beneficiary in the year of the claim is a second number
    and the second number <= 2.

section remedy is:

% The policy's own conditions of payment (Policy Article A52465, "Policy
% specific documentation requirements").
rule ko_documentation with provenance Policy Article A52465,
        confer "For a custom-fabricated orthosis, there must be documentation in the supplier's records to support the medical necessity of that type of device rather than a prefabricated orthosis":
the policy specific documentation requirements are met for a claim
    if the policy of the claim is knee_orthoses
    and the claim is for an item
    and the knee examination documentation is met for the item
    and the knee custom fabrication documentation is met for the item
    and the knee claim line diagnosis requirement is met for the claim.

% L1832, L1833, L1850 provided for knee instability: the laxity tests and
% the examination findings.
rule ko_laxity_documentation with provenance Policy Article A52465,
        confer "The joint laxity test(s) performed; and, A description of the exam findings that support objective joint laxity":
the knee examination documentation is met for an item
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L1832", "L1833", "L1850"]
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the finding knee instability about the beneficiary is established
    and the medical record of the beneficiary documents the joint laxity tests performed on the knee
    and the medical record of the beneficiary documents examination findings supporting objective joint laxity.

% The rotation control orthoses managing instability: the ambulatory status
% and the examination.
rule ko_instability_documentation with provenance Policy Article A52465,
        confer "for the management of an ambulatory beneficiary with knee instability, the medical records must include documentation of all of the following: The beneficiary’s ambulatory status":
the knee examination documentation is met for an item
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L1843", "L1844", "L1845", "L1846", "L1851", "L1852"]
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the finding knee instability about the beneficiary is established
    and the medical record of the beneficiary documents the ambulatory status
    and the medical record of the beneficiary documents the joint laxity tests performed on the knee
    and the medical record of the beneficiary documents examination findings supporting objective joint laxity.

% The rotation control orthoses managing osteoarthritis: the ambulatory
% status, the symptoms, the examination, the imaging report.
rule ko_osteoarthritis_documentation with provenance Policy Article A52465,
        confer "An imaging report (e.g., x-ray, CT scan, MRI) that describes arthritic changes (e.g., joint space narrowing, bone spurs, cysts) consistent with medial or lateral compartment tibiofemoral osteoarthritis":
the knee examination documentation is met for an item
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L1843", "L1844", "L1845", "L1846", "L1851", "L1852"]
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the osteoarthritis criteria for the item
    and the medical record of the beneficiary documents the ambulatory status
    and the medical record of the beneficiary documents the symptoms due to tibiofemoral osteoarthritis
    and the medical record of the beneficiary documents a physical examination of the knee
    and the medical record of the beneficiary includes an imaging report describing arthritic changes of the knee.

% After a recent injury or surgery the Article names no documentation of its
% own: a device of this model
rule ko_injury_documentation:
the knee examination documentation is met for an item
    if the item is a knee orthosis with examination documentation
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary has had a recent injury to the knee.

% any other code: a device of this model
rule ko_no_examination_documentation:
the knee examination documentation is met for an item
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and it is not the case that
        the item is a knee orthosis with examination documentation.

rule ko_orthotist_records with provenance Policy Article A52465,
        confer "This information will be corroborated by the functional evaluation in the orthotist’s records":
the knee custom fabrication documentation is met for an item
    if the item is a custom fabricated knee orthosis
    and the records of the orthotist include a functional evaluation corroborating the need for custom fabrication of the item.

% a prefabricated orthosis: a device of this model
rule ko_no_custom_documentation:
the knee custom fabrication documentation is met for an item
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and it is not the case that
        the item is a custom fabricated knee orthosis.

rule ko_claim_line_diagnosis with provenance Policy Article A52465,
        confer "The supplier must include on the claim line the diagnosis code(s) for HCPCS codes L1830, L1831, L1832, L1833, L1834, L1836, L1840, L1843, L1844, L1845, L1846, L1850, L1851, L1852 and L1860":
the knee claim line diagnosis requirement is met for a claim
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is a knee orthosis requiring the diagnosis code on the claim line
    and the claim states the diagnosis code of the beneficiary.

% an addition or a replacement interface: a device of this model
rule ko_no_claim_line_diagnosis:
the knee claim line diagnosis requirement is met for a claim
    if the claim is for an item
    and it is not the case that
        the item is a knee orthosis requiring the diagnosis code on the claim line.
